  {
   "title": "Rule 1: use the infinitive",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "After a pseudo verb, use **only the infinitive** form of the main verb, with any of the affixes **-um-**, **mag-**, **-in-** and **-hin**. Do not use the past, present or future."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "",
      "Sentence"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Correct",
       "Dapat **kumáin** ng gulay ang mga batà.  (*The children must eat [their] vegetables.*)"
      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Dapat kumákain ng gulay ang mga batà."
      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Dapat kákain ng gulay ang mga batà."
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Dapat + kumáin"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "",
      "Sentence"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Correct",
       "Kailángang **punuín** mo ng batò ang pasô.  (*You must fill up the claypot with stones.*)"
      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Kailángang pupunuín mo ng batò ang pasô."
      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Kailángang napunô mo ng batò ang pasô."
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Kailángan + punuín"
    },
    {
     "type": "h",
     "t": "Ligatures"
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Notice the ligature **-g** that links **kailangan** to the main verb **punuin** (Lesson 7: -g after n). Other pseudo verbs take ligatures too."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "rule",
     "title": "When is a ligature needed?",
     "items": [
      "With **ibig**, **áyaw** and **dápat** placed directly **before a main verb**, a ligature is **not necessary**: *Dápat kumáin…*",
      "But **every** pseudo verb that is followed by a **pronoun** (such as **siyá** or **niyá**) needs a ligature **after the pronoun**: *Dápat siyáng…*, *Áyaw niláng…*"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Rule 2: ibig and gustó take ko, mo…",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "With **ibig** and **gustó**, use the possessive pronoun that comes **after** a noun (such as **ko** and **mo**, from Lesson 8), and attach the right ligature: **ko + ng = kong**."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Place the pronoun **between** the pseudo verb and the main verb. This works whether the main verb is **active** (-um- or mag-) or **passive** (-in-)."
    },
    {
     "type": "pattern",
     "title": "Pseudo verb + pronoun + ligature + main verb",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Active",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "Ibig",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "ko",
         "r": "poss"
        },
        {
         "t": "-ng",
         "r": "link"
        },
        {
         "t": "mag-áral",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "ng Tagálog",
         "r": "noun"
        }
       ]
      },
