      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Gustó arálin ko ng Tagálog."
      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Gustó arálin ng Tagálog ako."
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Ibig and gustó"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "english",
     "title": "ng or ang after the main verb?",
     "t": "Look closely: with the active **mag-áral** the object takes **ng** (*ng Tagálog*); with the passive **arálin** it takes **ang** (*ang Tagálog*), just as in Lessons 15 and 16."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Rule 3: the other pseudo verbs",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Except for ibig and gustó**, the pseudo verbs need a **nominative pronoun** (such as **akó** or **siyá**) with a ligature when the main verb is **active** (-um- or mag-)."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "",
      "Sentence"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Correct",
       "Dápat **siyáng uminóm** ng gátas."
      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Dápat siyáng inumín ang gátas."
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Active verb: siyá"
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "In the same way, a pseudo verb needs a **possessive pronoun** (such as **niyá**) with a ligature when the main verb is a **passive -in** verb."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "",
      "Sentence"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Correct",
       "Dápat **niyáng inumín** ang gátas."
      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Dápat niyáng uminóm ng gátas."
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Passive verb: niyá"
    },
