        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "note": "Active -um-/mag- verb: akó, siyá… Passive -in- verb: niyá, ko…"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "remember",
     "title": "Pronoun check",
     "items": [
      "**Ibig / gustó**: always the after-noun possessive (kong, mong…).",
      "**Other pseudo verbs + active verb**: nominative pronoun (akóng, siyáng…).",
      "**Other pseudo verbs + -in- verb**: possessive pronoun (niyáng…)."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Rule 4: endings",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "A pseudo verb that ends in a **consonant other than n** does **not** need a suffix. Pseudo verbs ending in a **vowel** need one: the ligature **-ng**."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "",
      "Sentence"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Correct",
       "**Ibig** uminóm ng gátas ang batà."
      ],
      [
       "Correct",
       "**Gustóng** uminóm ng gátas ang batà."
      ],
      [
       "Incorrect",
       "Gustó uminóm ng gátas ang batà."
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Ibig (ends in g) and gustó (ends in a vowel)"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Why",
     "t": "**Ibig** ends in **g**, so nothing is added. **Gustó** ends in the vowel **o**, so it becomes **gustóng**. Compare **Puwédeng lutúin** and **Kailángang maligò** above: puwéde ends in a vowel (-ng) and kailángan ends in n (-g)."
    }
   ]
